{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority","id":1409126,"title":"What if Wan Gui were the dominant Group of Vampires and Cainites the minority?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-19T06:55:25-07:00","id":1409126,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What if Wan Gui were the dominant Group of Vampires and Cainites the minority?","content":"So I like me a good alternate setting, like what if the Fae were the lords of the supernatural world and the others operated under them, or what if aliens had a secret war against the supernaturals of earth. This is in the same Vein. What if the Wan Gui were the dominant and default group of Vampires. They spread out around the entire world so thoroughly that essentially all of humanity inherited their Karmic debt so Wan Gui could appear anywhere. They would use the default Term Hungry Dead, but like how Kindred seemed to center around European tradition, the Hungry Dead centered around Asia due to their historical roots there. The most common powerful elders are from Asia but they have been around the world long enough that Ancestors come from all cultures.<br /> <br /> And the brood of Caine is a minority that spread through the embrace. They might have a few centers of power like say the British Isles, and Rome and Sicily but most places they are treated as outsiders or possibly even hunted on sight. Thus Cainite Disciplines are the mysterious and rare powers while the Shintai have expanded and specialized and have become a robust set of options.<br /> <br /> How does this play out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T07:40:38-07:00","id":1409133,"title":"","content":"This only works under the assumption that Cainites have lost all/most of their ancients and elders, thus they are all high generation and can only reproduce so much. The Cathayans can rise up on their own, whilst the Cainites must eat their way up, and if there's nobody to eat, the Cathayans will have a much higher power ceiling than the Cainites, allowing them to destroy most cainites outside of a few cities where vampires do have some older blood and have a good defence. Cainites, in adapting to this threat, probably aren't that canibalistic; They are going to trust their elders to shelter them from an external threat. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, if vampires are to keep their ancients; they'd win wars. Quite simply they can produce way, way faster than Cathayans and have better control over mortal populaces. Many Wan Gui, raised in western cultures, would probably have mercenary or good relationships with Cainites. <br /> <br /> Also... &quot;Cainites&quot; won big in part because europeans conquered near everything. If the Cathayans still used asia as their hub the implications would be for an alt-history were asia was the colonizer for the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T07:45:20-07:00","id":1409135,"title":"","content":"It would be like every early 90's cyberpunk dystopia where Asian based MegaCorps own everything. It would be amazing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T09:26:02-07:00","id":1409150,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue with Cainites being a minority and the Kuei-jin being the majority comes down to population replenishment.<br /> <br /> A Kuei-jin must have lived a relatively complete mortal life, have squandered that life in some way that sets them up to go to hell, then finally have the psychological fortitude to escape the Yomi and return to earth. All of that can take between 16 and 70 years wait between the next Kuei-Jin popping up and that is assuming minimal time in the Yomi. On the other hand the Cainites can just choose to embrace who ever has the skills and attributes they want. So you need some mechanical reason for why Cainites can't mass embrace or even just embrace at a rate faster than the Kuei-Jin pop up.<br /> <br /> Once the Cainite exponential population problem is taken care of we can focus on looking at history to explain the movements across the globe. For instance there seems to be evidence pointing to the idea that some Chinese explorers managed to find the west coast of the US a couple centuries before Columbus hopped across the pond, but due to political upheaval in China when they got back, no colonization or further exploration was planned. So that gives you Kuei-jin access to the new world to spread their influence.<br /> <br /> The heritage restriction that only allows asians to become Kuei-Jin makes storytelling certain character concepts less viable with a world spanning focus. Instead the Kuei-Jin should probably pull a 1980s approach and just have massive asian corporations that span the globe. Kind of like how in the movie &quot;Bright&quot; all the really high end CEOs and rich people are Elves. This would facilitate certain dharma shifts, like how the Face of the Gods dharma would probably be one of the most prominent groups if for no other reason they are one of the best at controlling groups of mortals in the Kuei-Jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:26:08-07:00","id":1409207,"title":"","content":"Well Asians only become Hungry Ghosts because Yomi wan has access to only about half the souls in there Metaphysical paradigm and that coincides with the half of the world Wan Xian governed in prehistory. This assumes the Wan Gui have claimed Dragons Nests around the world and for long enough the metaphysical territory of Yomi wan has become global.<br /> <br /> This also effects the numbers as more Wan Gui rise. Let\u2019s assume they have even a slight overpopulation problem and thus have no issue with replenishing their numbers unless they lose a drastic amount of their population all at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:35:40-07:00","id":1409210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409133#post1409133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This only works under the assumption that Cainites have lost all/most of their ancients and elders, thus they are all high generation and can only reproduce so much. The Cathayans can rise up on their own, whilst the Cainites must eat their way up, and if there's nobody to eat, the Cathayans will have a much higher power ceiling than the Cainites, allowing them to destroy most cainites outside of a few cities where vampires do have some older blood and have a good defence. Cainites, in adapting to this threat, probably aren't that canibalistic; They are going to trust their elders to shelter them from an external threat. <br /> <br /> Otherwise, if vampires are to keep their ancients; they'd win wars. Quite simply they can produce way, way faster than Cathayans and have better control over mortal populaces. Many Wan Gui, raised in western cultures, would probably have mercenary or good relationships with Cainites. <br /> <br /> Also... &amp;quot;Cainites&amp;quot; won big in part because europeans conquered near everything. If the Cathayans still used asia as their hub the implications would be for an alt-history were asia was the colonizer for the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the idea would be the Cainites and the Wan Gui probably warred centuries if not millenia ago and the Cainites lost, maybe the Antes died fighting the Arhats and most of the methuselah were wiped out. The remaining Cainites don\u2019t have very good generation except for a handful. If they got territory they could replenish numbers but not cure their generation problem that easily but they don\u2019t have the time or safety to mass train enough neonates for a quadrupling of their population. Meanwhile the Wan Gui recovered their loss of elders from the war naturally centuries ago.<br /> <br /> Presumably some of the internal conflicts would be Things the Quincunx trying reign in and dominate the Sunset Courts and various civil Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:38:42-07:00","id":1409212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409207#post1409207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Asians only become Hungry Ghosts because Yomi wan has access to only about half the souls in there Metaphysical paradigm and that coincides with the half of the world Wan Xian governed in prehistory. This assumes the Wan Gui have claimed Dragons Nests around the world and for long enough the metaphysical territory of Yomi wan has become global.<br /> <br /> This also effects the numbers as more Wan Gui rise. Let\u2019s assume they have even a slight overpopulation problem and thus have no issue with replenishing their numbers unless they lose a drastic amount of their population all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably because I missed a thing or two when I read the core book (And have only read the core book) I always figured becoming a Wan Kuei was a matter of geography not anything particular to do with the ethinicity of a person or the nature of the soul.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:48:40-07:00","id":1409213,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine the remaining Cainites would be servants of Yomi,<br /> maybe cainite drones as well,<br /> we'd have cainites on path of revelations or path of night spreading evil among humanity for yomi to harvest","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T14:28:12-07:00","id":1409221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409133#post1409133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This only works under the assumption that Cainites have lost all/most of their ancients and elders, thus they are all high generation and can only reproduce so much. The Cathayans can rise up on their own, whilst the Cainites must eat their way up, and if there's nobody to eat, the Cathayans will have a much higher power ceiling than the Cainites, allowing them to destroy most cainites outside of a few cities where vampires do have some older blood and have a good defence. Cainites, in adapting to this threat, probably aren't that canibalistic; They are going to trust their elders to shelter them from an external threat.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, if vampires are to keep their ancients; they'd win wars. Quite simply they can produce way, way faster than Cathayans and have better control over mortal populaces. Many Wan Gui, raised in western cultures, would probably have mercenary or good relationships with Cainites.<br /> <br /> Also... &quot;Cainites&quot; won big in part because europeans conquered near everything. If the Cathayans still used asia as their hub the implications would be for an alt-history were asia was the colonizer for the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would Still only work if they also lost all rituals that allowed one to increase their gen without diablerie(like the assamite &quot;From Marduk's Throat&quot; ritual). Those are supposed to be uber-rare and closely guarded secrets, but elder vampires are Also supposed to be uber-rare and I'm pretty sure loosing their ancients would be enough to persuade many a vampire clan to start using their rituals more Liberally(just to survive if nothing else).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T14:48:09-07:00","id":1409227,"title":"","content":"They are? I mean if you look at it from a Noneurocentric view of the world Kindred have always been a minor issue. For most of human history most of humanity has fallen under WK domination. There were whole cities in &quot;Medievial&quot; china that a larger population than the equivalent time period in England. In the Blink of an Elder's eye Kindred have come to matter. Europe has come to matter... but China endures.<br /> <br /> And look at the 21st Century.... the powers of the West wane.. while China Ascends. What is 200 years to an Immortal being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T14:53:11-07:00","id":1409228,"title":"","content":"Interesting Idea:<br /> <br /> MyWoD works on the assumption that for hundreds of thousands of years Hungry Dead were the only type of 'vampire' around the world, and then 20K years ago in Northern Africa someones Second Breath went terribly wrong ( right?) and the Kindred came about, a form of Hungry Dead that spread not through fighting your way out of the dark but as plague. Soon Kindred spread across first Africa then the Middle East and Europe swamping and destroying the old Ghost Families......more recently they have spread to North America, Australia, South Asia, SE Asia. East Asia, South America, Central America, Indo-China....the Hungry Dead still hold on in these places but <span style=\"color:#878787\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">inexorably</span></span> they are increasing in numbers. In places where the Hungry Dead are still strong and the Kindred relatively few agreements are made and the societies mingle and join...but it is a cordiality born of necessity and if the balance tips....the Kindred will spawn like cockroaches and take another territory as their own.<br /> <br /> I will admit to preferring KotE Mechanics and metaphysics over VtM ones simply because I prefer folkloric 'vampires' over cinematic ones and while VtM does media-inspired vampires very well KotE is a much better system for modelling even such traditional European beings as Moroi, Shtriga, Draugr, Gjenganger, Pijavica and more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:03:06-07:00","id":1409230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409150#post1409150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance there seems to be evidence pointing to the idea that some Chinese explorers managed to find the west coast of the US a couple centuries before Columbus hopped across the pond, but due to political upheaval in China when they got back, no colonization or further exploration was planned.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Just no.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T21:57:11-07:00","id":1409291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409230#post1409230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Just no.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I appreciate brevity, after a certain point you have to go a little more in depth in your responses.<br /> <br /> Because there are several examples of story hook worthy material in history that can be used as explanations for the home brew setting justification. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Viking_landing.jpg/1280px-Viking_landing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories\" target=\"_blank\"> Pre-Columbian transoceanic contact theories - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T22:12:25-07:00","id":1409293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409230#post1409230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Just no.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Actually, no, it's a legitimate theory. So are African explorers. We also know Vikings made it before the World's Worst Navigator.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T22:13:10-07:00","id":1409294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409291#post1409291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I appreciate brevity, after a certain point you have to go a little more in depth in your responses.<br /> <br /> Because there are several examples of story hook worthy material in history that can be used as explanations for the home brew setting justification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Viking_landing.jpg/1280px-Viking_landing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories\" target=\"_blank\"> Pre-Columbian transoceanic contact theories - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I remember the theory that Chinese vessels made contact with the west coast was torn apart by a lot of legitimate historians, and the author famous for bringing the theory to mainstream notice turned out to be a charlatan. I'm sure a number of youtube videos on the subject are easily found. But it is an interesting idea, especially for a setting like the World of Darkness. It could even explain a lack of Cainites north of Mexico by the time Cainites arrived from Europe, like secret groups of Wan Gui could have formed an underground court in America, capturing enough Holy sites to convert to Dragon Nests and trickle in enough replacement Wan Gui from the homeland and maybe from regions converted enough to Middle Kingdom Geomancy that mortals sometimes pop back from Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T09:00:03-07:00","id":1409361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409293#post1409293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">World's Worst Navigator.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Columbus was pretty reasonable with his navigation given historical context; Most people at that time thought the world was round (what a mistake) but assumed the earth's size was lot smaller than it is, he made the assumption that he reached the of 'south east of india' when deciding on the name 'indians', and with information exchange being what it is it's not unreasonable to confuse the strange exotic people you found with the strange exotic people you were hoping to find. It was pretty impressive he managed to cross the ocean so many times and find the colonies he had found before too. Good guy? No, but far from the worst navigator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T09:44:56-07:00","id":1409371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409361#post1409361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Columbus was pretty reasonable with his navigation given historical context; Most people at that time thought the world was round (what a mistake) but assumed the earth's size was lot smaller than it is, he made the assumption that he reached the of 'south east of india' when deciding on the name 'indians', and with information exchange being what it is it's not unreasonable to confuse the strange exotic people you found with the strange exotic people you were hoping to find. It was pretty impressive he managed to cross the ocean so many times and find the colonies he had found before too. Good guy? No, but far from the worst navigator.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Honestly we need to blame Marco Polo more for this bullshit. Since if you used the measurements from his travels you.. got Japan roughly where Cuba is.<br /> <br /> This is why even after they discovered this new land mass they gave the Pacific the name... the Peaceful ocean because they thought it was small and peaceful rather htan the world's largest oceans. Its why Magellan thought he was going to make it across in,. 2 weeks. Good maps were functionally state secrets until relatively modern times.<br /> <br /> However for all that.. columbus' plan worked. It took a couple more discoveries but the whole transfer the spices of asia through Mexico to the Old world worked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T10:45:00-07:00","id":1409381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409291#post1409291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I appreciate brevity, after a certain point you have to go a little more in depth in your responses.<br /> <br /> Because there are several examples of story hook worthy material in history that can be used as explanations for the home brew setting justification.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Columbian_trans-oceanic_contact_theories\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Co...ntact_theories</a><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409293#post1409293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Actually, no, it's a legitimate theory. So are African explorers. We also know Vikings made it before the World's Worst Navigator.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It is <b>not</b> a legitimate historical theory, any more than von Daniken is legitimate archeology. In fact, comparing them is something of a slight to von Daniken!<br /> <br /> The person who wrote most of it, Menziers, is not a researcher. He dropped out of school at 15, joined the navy and got advised to leave later for incompetence. He tried to write a book about China, his publisher told him it was unpublishable and asked him to write about China discovering America. It has been thoroughly debunked by serious historians, in words you do not normally see in scholarship and which I will not repeat.<br /> <br /> There is no research, no scholarship and in fact, no theory there.<br /> <br /> I mean, just at a glance, the pacific is way larger than the Atlantic. The distance from China to the west coast of America is twice as far as Colombus sailed. With no knowledge of sources of water, currents or prevailing winds a ship run by a vaguely competent Captain would need to get to America while still well before his halfway mark on water and provisions.<br /> <br /> The voyages of Zeng He are well attested historically. We know he made it to East Africa, Arabia, and many locations in Southeast Asia. He did not sail to Italy and start the renaissance, circumnavigate Greenland, sail the Northeast Passage, or any of the rest of the 1421 nonsense.<br /> The Norse are factual. As is Polynesian-American contacts both ways, and Inuit peoples, and there is a wisp of DNA related to Australian Aboriginals in a very few Amazon tribes. We can speculate about Japanese and Northeast Asian contacts and it'll be plausible but without evidence.<br /> <br /> The internet is sooo good for fake knowledge. It is ok to speculate on things like unknown contacts, what ifs or lost history. Just don't present it as facts or legitimate research! Science denialism is doing well enough on its own.<br /> <br /> None of which are to say that there could not have been contacts in the WoD. It is, after all supposed to contain individuals and organizations with vastly greater powers and resources than our world, and secret histories are par for the course there. I am just objecting to it being presented as real history in our world.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 08-20-2020, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T11:33:16-07:00","id":1409397,"title":"","content":"kuei jin have access to the umbra,<br /> do they even need sailors to to reach the continent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T13:52:26-07:00","id":1409413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409397#post1409397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kuei jin have access to the umbra,<br /> do they even need sailors to to reach the continent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would they want to? From their perspective they are the only people living in Civilization. They call their set up the &quot;Middle Kingdom&quot; for a reason. its not super crazy to think any place outside of the Middle Kingdom was a worthless backwater until the last couple hundred years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T13:49:52-07:00","id":1409622,"title":"","content":"So, I'd probably go in a slightly different direcion.<br /> <br /> For example, why aren't Cainites dominant, considering they are contagious and the Wan Gui are not? There could be several reasons. Maybe the Embrace doesn't work on everyone. For some reason or other, only a fraction of attempts actually work out, meaning that any Cainite who wishes to sire will lose Humanity fast as she leaves a string of corpses behind.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps in this world, Cainite blood becomes too watery with a high generation. Say, anything below seventh. Meaning that there are only few Cainites around, but at the same time, each and every one of them is a power unto herself. In a reversal of the shameless orientalism of the original KotE, now those Cain-born bloodsuckers are the thing to be feared... at least in secret.<br /> <br /> Maybe only particular Clans survived. Those with the best skills at hiding, and/or those with Obfuscate. Now it becomes difficult to eradicate them because it's so hard to find them first. Or, say there are no Lupines around; instead, it's the feral Cainite Clans who lurk in the wilderness. Perhaps through (un)natural selection, they became able to survive on animal blood just fine.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps some ancient vampire, be it one of the more mystical Antes or a Wan Gui, tore the barriers between life and the afterlife. In the aftermath, Yomi expanded to cover most of the world\u2014except for those pockets, where Caine's get was sucked into the Lands of the Dead, where they had to learn how to feed on dead souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T14:43:31-07:00","id":1409628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409622#post1409622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'd probably go in a slightly different direcion.<br /> <br /> For example, why aren't Cainites dominant, considering they are contagious and the Wan Gui are not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wan Gui have the spirit worlds to their advantage,<br /> they have better ways of blending in with humanity,<br /> they are immune to blood bonds and diablerie,<br /> they can resist mind control,<br /> and they are less antagonised by other supernaturals<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409413#post1409413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why would they want to? From their perspective they are the only people living in Civilization. They call their set up the &quot;Middle Kingdom&quot; for a reason. its not super crazy to think any place outside of the Middle Kingdom was a worthless backwater until the last couple hundred years.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but here we're talking about kuei jin being dominant and spread across the world,<br /> <br /> why would they want to spread out? any reason you want,<br /> kuei-jin explorers, youngsters wishing to escape their oppressive elders, hertical dharmas moving away from the dominant dharmas etc<br /> <br /> that's, of course, if we consider hungy dead only pop-up in Asia,<br /> we could just have the 1000 hells covering most of the globe, or the 1000 hells are not the only hells people can escape from","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 08-21-2020, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T17:17:00-07:00","id":1409655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409628#post1409628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wan Gui have the spirit worlds to their advantage,<br /> they have better ways of blending in with humanity,<br /> they are immune to blood bonds and diablerie,<br /> they can resist mind control,<br /> and they are less antagonised by other supernaturals<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> yeah, but here we're talking about kuei jin being dominant and spread across the world,<br /> <br /> why would they want to spread out? any reason you want,<br /> kuei-jin explorers, youngsters wishing to escape their oppressive elders, hertical dharmas moving away from the dominant dharmas etc<br /> <br /> that's, of course, if we consider hungy dead only pop-up in Asia,<br /> we could just have the 1000 hells covering most of the globe, or the 1000 hells are not the only hells people can escape from</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are also possible. Looking at reasons from the Cainite and the Wan Gui perspective at the same time is not at all mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> We should as well consider, as you alluded, how many of the Hungry Dead outside Asia actually follow Wan Gui ideology, or fall into the paradigm. There are plenty Cainites around who believe in a totally different origin of vampire-kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:53:31-07:00","id":1409682,"title":"","content":"Push the Wan Xian's fall from grace far enough back into prehistory and the ancestors of Native Americans were carrying the karmic debt with them when they crossed the land bridge into Alaska. Push it far enough back and the ancestors of every human tribe and nation were carrying it before they left Africa. That's part's easy - it's just a matter of how far you want to turn the dial.<br /> <br /> If China remains the cultural capital for this kind of undead in this setting, it can easily be chalked up to population density and China's phenomenal history of being able to hold a culturally coherent empire together for millennia.<br /> <br /> Conjuring up a mechanical reason why the Kindred variety of vampire hasn't become as universal could take a little work, but that's an opportunity to have some fun tinkering. <br /> <br /> Maybe they have the Ghouls' weakness that their true age catches up with them if they don't feed, making torpor deadly for an elder who isn't influential enough to ensure that he's fed while he sleeps. This ensures millennia of generational turnover that makes an individual Kindred a relatively fleeting blip on history's radar.<br /> <br /> I'd assume that Kindred are not treated as true heirs of Cain's (without the &quot;e&quot;) Old Testament punishment in this setting and have some other origin, even if it's shrouded in mystery or lost to the ages. That gives you some freedom to play with the concepts and mechanics of Generation. Maybe the raw power of Kindred is capped at the equivalent of Eighth Generation, reflecting a spiritual deadness that prevents them from having anything remotely resembling a Bodhisattva among them. <br /> <br /> Both options have the benefit of making it much easier for rival supernaturals to cull the numbers of troublesome Kindred. It also completely justifies the belief among some Ventrue elders that other supernaturals are holding them back.<br /> <br /> It all really depends on what you feel like you need to keep and what you're willing to deconstruct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-21-2020, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T05:06:51-07:00","id":1409737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409150#post1409150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The heritage restriction that only allows asians to become Kuei-Jin makes storytelling certain character concepts less viable with a world spanning focus. Instead the Kuei-Jin should probably pull a 1980s approach and just have massive asian corporations that span the globe. Kind of like how in the movie &quot;Bright&quot; all the really high end CEOs and rich people are Elves. This would facilitate certain dharma shifts, like how the Face of the Gods dharma would probably be one of the most prominent groups if for no other reason they are one of the best at controlling groups of mortals in the Kuei-Jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did come with a solution of my own to the &quot;heritage issue&quot; in my own games when i decided to do a rewrite of sorts of the Wan Kuei/Gui Ren.<br /> That said, it was partly made to tie more closely both kinds of vampires and made some major elements of KotE quite clearly wrong.<br /> (But then the Book of Nod is also quite utterly in a number of issues too in my games, so definitely no big deal)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T10:16:54-07:00","id":1409781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409622#post1409622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example, why aren't Cainites dominant, considering they are contagious and the Wan Gui are not? .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To put it another way, you can stamp out a disease. You can't stamp out Winter. If you killed every Wan Gui in the world tomorrow the next night.. new wan Gui would rise. If you killed every Kindred in the world That's it. Its over forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kindred by their nature hit a malthusian limit then eat each other. Its a testament to the Farsighteness of kindred that there's anything resembling a Kindred society.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409628#post1409628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> yeah, but here we're talking about kuei jin being dominant and spread across the world,<br /> <br /> why would they want to spread out? any reason you want,<br /> kuei-jin explorers, youngsters wishing to escape their oppressive elders, hertical dharmas moving away from the dominant dharmas etc<br /> <br /> that's, of course, if we consider hungy dead only pop-up in Asia,<br /> we could just have the 1000 hells covering most of the globe, or the 1000 hells are not the only hells people can escape from</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The point I am trying to make is controlling the largest population centers on the planet along with what could be seen for most of human history as the most advanced civilizations on the planet doesn't look like people who aren't a dominant force but rather the last couple hundred years have been at odds with the greater pattern of history and that greater pattern seems to be reasserting itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T12:16:33-07:00","id":1409796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409781#post1409781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point I am trying to make is controlling the largest population centers on the planet along with what could be seen for most of human history as the most advanced civilizations on the planet doesn't look like people who aren't a dominant force but rather the last couple hundred years have been at odds with the greater pattern of history and that greater pattern seems to be reasserting itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>fair enough, but I'd still insist for them to have stronholds in the west,<br /> Vampire is a game played mostly on the local level,<br /> if a cainite can walk through the whole american continent without having ever thinking about the hungry dead, then the feeling of dominion just isn't there<br /> <br /> to give you an example,<br /> the sabbat had the most territorial (and by extension population) control in the American continent,<br /> but the Camarilla was still the &quot;dominant&quot; faction in the continent,<br /> all that thanks to their stronholds and their influence in the corporate landscape and the media,<br /> the sabbat had Mexico, but the mexican corps were more Camarilla than sabbat,<br /> sabbat had Canada, but the Candian media had ventrue influence<br /> <br /> that's how it should be for kuei-jin,<br /> remember that we're not just talking about them being dominant but also them being spread out around the world","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T16:38:10-07:00","id":1409832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409796#post1409796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> fair enough, but I'd still insist for them to have stronholds in the west,<br /> Vampire is a game played mostly on the local level,<br /> if a cainite can walk through the whole american continent without having ever thinking about the hungry dead, then the feeling of dominion just isn't there<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> a cainite can do that with Followrs of Set, Giovanni, changelings, Ghosts, werewolves... you don't need to hold giant areas of domination to matter on a local level. Hell there's a good chance a gangrel could wander the entirity of the American continent for centuries and never meet another vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> And holding giant areas of domination conversely don't really matter on a local level. The sabbat controls.. Mexico is no different than the Wan Gui control Japan if your game isn't set in Mexico or Japan. Air planes are a thing. Ships are a thing. The world is as big or as small as the sts makes it. A couple of KJ travel to protect their assets in your domain because of international commece is all you need to engage with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T18:43:39-07:00","id":1409993,"title":"","content":"Most folks seem to want to reinterpret Cainites as too weak to be any real challenge to the Wan Gui, both individually and as a whole. I'm the only one, or so it looks like, who'd imagine that if KotE is the core game, its tone would change as well. Away from the unquestioned(!) orientalism and arrogance; not presenting the Wan Gui as super-vampires, like Cainites only better. It took later instalments to get away from that, not helping that the VtM sourcebooks played it up as well. That's one major reason why I wondered if the Cainites still around in such a system would be presented as the dangerous, mysterious Other instead of pushovers.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps someone shares this sentiment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T21:42:13-07:00","id":1410010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1409993#post1409993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most folks seem to want to reinterpret Cainites as too weak to be any real challenge to the Wan Gui, both individually and as a whole. I'm the only one, or so it looks like, who'd imagine that if KotE is the core game, its tone would change as well. Away from the unquestioned(!) orientalism and arrogance; not presenting the Wan Gui as super-vampires, like Cainites only better. It took later instalments to get away from that, not helping that the VtM sourcebooks played it up as well. That's one major reason why I wondered if the Cainites still around in such a system would be presented as the dangerous, mysterious Other instead of pushovers.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps someone shares this sentiment?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On the contrary. I never understood the idea of Hungry Dead as uber vamps, mechanically Cainites get stronger faster and grow their disciplines far more readily than the Hungry Dead can. They are also much more physically robust over all unless the Hungry Ghost embraces their demon side completely.<br /> <br /> As a species Cainites have the ability to reproduce at an exponential rate and can create utterly loyal mortal+ armies essentially on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T22:54:43-07:00","id":1410017,"title":"","content":"Yeah and a lot Hungry Dead Disciplines are just Mechanically clunky. They don't have Auspex or Obfuscate, well I guess the Smoke Discipline kind of works as Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T02:52:08-07:00","id":1410029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410010#post1410010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On the contrary. I never understood the idea of Hungry Dead as uber vamps, mechanically Cainites get stronger faster and grow their disciplines far more readily than the Hungry Dead can. They are also much more physically robust over all unless the Hungry Ghost embraces their demon side completely.<br /> <br /> As a species Cainites have the ability to reproduce at an exponential rate and can create utterly loyal mortal+ armies essentially on a whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>hungry dead have fomori (which, iirc, are perfectly active during the day)<br /> <br /> and the demon shintai form causes delirium, so your army of mortals are gonna be stomping each other as they're running away in mad terror (a bit like what obtenebration does),<br /> that's assuming mortals can do anything about creatures that can jump in and out of reality,<br /> <br /> mass embrace is all well and good, if you have the vinculum to keep them under control,<br /> but it hurts the cainites as much as it hurts their enemies, since you're hurting the herds while creating more vampires thirsty for blood<br /> (that's why, by revised, the practice became less popular, but still necessary because cainites suck that way)<br /> <br /> imo, the only real good stuff cainites have would be blood magic, which is probably the best weapon against kuei-jin (or anything really),<br /> <br /> you can win a battle against hungry dead, but on an extended conflict, you'll be forced to resort to the blood mages or stuff like dark thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> <br /> anyway, we don't need kuei-jin to be uber vampires, since they can convince groups of cainites to joing their side (which is what they did in California),<br /> so they don't need to fight on their own<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T03:02:06-07:00","id":1410030,"title":"","content":"Yes indeed Cainites have Blood Sorcery, while Hungry Dead have Rites. But they don't have as many rites shown in the books, and they seem to be concentrated on their Undead Culture mixed with a little bit of the magic umph of the Garou Rites. They also seem to have more magical items then Kindred who usually restrict those things to their Sorcerers, or the Laibon's culture of magic Fetishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T04:01:29-07:00","id":1410034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410029#post1410029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> hungry dead have fomori (which, iirc, are perfectly active during the day)<br /> <br /> and the demon shintai form causes delirium, so your army of mortals are gonna be stomping each other as they're running away in mad terror (a bit like what obtenebration does),<br /> that's assuming mortals can do anything about creatures that can jump in and out of reality,<br /> <br /> mass embrace is all well and good, if you have the vinculum to keep them under control,<br /> but it hurts the cainites as much as it hurts their enemies, since you're hurting the herds while creating more vampires thirsty for blood<br /> (that's why, by revised, the practice became less popular, but still necessary because cainites suck that way)<br /> <br /> imo, the only real good stuff cainites have would be blood magic, which is probably the best weapon against kuei-jin (or anything really),<br /> <br /> you can win a battle against hungry dead, but on an extended conflict, you'll be forced to resort to the blood mages or stuff like dark thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> <br /> anyway, we don't need kuei-jin to be uber vampires, since they can convince groups of cainites to joing their side (which is what they did in California),<br /> so they don't need to fight on their own</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well only a small portion of Hungry Dead have Fomori/Bakemono/Mockeries...where as every Cainite worth their salt has a bunch of ghouls. Hungry Dead rely a lot more on Scarlet Screens, mortal protectors who are only somewhat in the know.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are immune to Delerium.<br /> <br /> Cainite disciplines are cheap, more powerful at low levels and much less resource intensive. Umbral movement is a plus but difficult in cities.<br /> <br /> The main advantage Kindred have is it takes a year or more to replace a young Hungry Dead, whereas it takes a day or maybe a couple of days to make a new Cainite.<br /> <br /> If Hungry Dead have time to prepare and call on spirit allies and rites then they can give a good accounting of themselves, very true. The more powerful among them can roflstomp the Tremere at their own game given prep time.<br /> <br /> But Kindred get pretty much every advantage cheaper, quicker and with less investment.<br /> <br /> Which is why Hungry Dead maintain good relations with other Night Folk if they can....because its always good to have useful favours to call on.<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, favours and shadow alliances win the day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T06:37:44-07:00","id":1410049,"title":"","content":"neonates may have only one or two ghouls. I don't think it's a mistake that the starting amount of retainers is capped at 5. But also neonates, having more powerful social disciplines earlier on, and are more likely/more capable of cultivating wealth. <br /> <br /> But the real problem I have witht the above post: It takes four-five turns to make a cainite, assuming we're working with adults (RAW, It'd take three turns to make a cainite with a child; Grab, Drink, Drink+embrace.) a few more turns if you don't have a food source at the ready and want to feed them. You can educate them en-mass if you feel like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T07:01:06-07:00","id":1410054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410049#post1410049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">neonates may have only one or two ghouls. I don't think it's a mistake that the starting amount of retainers is capped at 5. But also neonates, having more powerful social disciplines earlier on, and are more likely/more capable of cultivating wealth.<br /> <br /> But the real problem I have witht the above post: It takes four-five turns to make a cainite, assuming we're working with adults (RAW, It'd take three turns to make a cainite with a child; Grab, Drink, Drink+embrace.) a few more turns if you don't have a food source at the ready and want to feed them. You can educate them en-mass if you feel like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hoho what could go wrong with a mass embraced shovelhead kindergarden. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T07:40:25-07:00","id":1410059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410017#post1410017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah and a lot Hungry Dead Disciplines are just Mechanically clunky. They don't have Auspex or Obfuscate, well I guess the Smoke Discipline kind of works as Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I agree that the mechanics for KotE are clunky, they are not without function. For example the first dot in Yin Prana turns you invisible and silent, unlike Obfuscate which is a mental projection to not be noticed, Shrouded Moon apparently affects light and sound directly. Chi Uh Muh on the other hand is the closest to Auspex, especially once you factor in all the different perks from sight types all given by Chi Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T08:10:38-07:00","id":1410066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410010#post1410010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the contrary. I never understood the idea of Hungry Dead as uber vamps, mechanically Cainites get stronger faster and grow their disciplines far more readily than the Hungry Dead can. They are also much more physically robust over all unless the Hungry Ghost embraces their demon side completely.<br /> <br /> As a species Cainites have the ability to reproduce at an exponential rate and can create utterly loyal mortal+ armies essentially on a whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE is a very clunky system that doesn't lend itself to a casual review. Most of its powers and systems are locked away in the secondary systems or how they interact. Thus many white room comparisons fall short due to only a surface reading been done or a lack of alternate parameters being considered.<br /> <br /> Also since Kuei-jin don't function off of a clan system like Cainites, you have no clue what the true power level of your encounter actually is. The Hungry Dead you are interacting with might be newly risen and civilized devil freshly indoctrinated into a given dharma or they could be a few thousand years old with all the xp and additional power that goes along with that, but recently had an epiphany which lead them to switch dharmas and thus currently is low ranked in their new dharma.<br /> <br /> Kuei-jin are very powerful because they give options for doing things from completely different angles rather than head on. I mean sure you might have a cainite power growth curve that is steeper, but the kuei-jin will be able to do things only a cainite specialist can counter. For example most Kuei-jin can deal with spirits, but the only cainite that can do that is a necromancer.<br /> <br /> KotE was designed to be a kitchen sink cross over system, so the Kuei-jin have a little bit of everything thrown into them. So as an example if you go up against a Devil Tiger you have no clue if you are going to be dealing with a Demon Shintai &amp; Iron Mountain specialist that can go toe to toe with most cainite combat builds or if you will be dealing with an Artificer who has a few dozen jade artifacts / fetishes that basically triple their chi pools and gives the artificer access to spirit charms which run on different rules than disciplines do.<br /> <br /> Then add in the ability to produce dhampyrs who can wield Joss Manipulation and things get really interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T08:10:40-07:00","id":1410067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410034#post1410034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cainite disciplines are cheap, more powerful at low levels and much less resource intensive. Umbral movement is a plus but difficult in cities.<br /> <br /> The main advantage Kindred have is it takes a year or more to replace a young Hungry Dead, whereas it takes a day or maybe a couple of days to make a new Cainite.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>just remember that kj have innate celerity and potence, before even considering their disciplines<br /> <br /> you should also check the stat blocks for shovelheads and other young cainites in Midnight Siege and Mexico by night,<br /> they can reproduce quickly, but a new cainite is nowhere near as deadly as a new kj,<br /> unless your starting cainite has obtenebration 5 or protean 5 or something<br /> <br /> the balancing factor would be that cainites have less trouble with chi economy than young kj","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 08-24-2020, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T08:25:43-07:00","id":1410071,"title":"","content":"Wan Gui is a crossover thing, Vampire, Werewolf and Wraith. But it melts them bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T08:29:22-07:00","id":1410074,"title":"","content":"Doesn't matter how great KJ powers synergize: Cainites, if they're willing, can easily set the stage to be 2 versus 1, or 3 vs 1, or if they can branch out and make it 5 vs 1, or 10 vs 1, or 30 to 1 if they're really desperate. So long as there are people and one cainite remains alive, they can replace their losses. This is why the individually superior Garou avoid wars with vampires. If the KJ start sending men at the Cainites, they're just handing them soldiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T08:38:51-07:00","id":1410075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410074#post1410074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't matter how great KJ powers synergize: Cainites, if they're willing, can easily set the stage to be 2 versus 1, or 3 vs 1, or if they can branch out and make it 5 vs 1, or 10 vs 1, or 30 to 1 if they're really desperate. So long as there are people and one cainite remains alive, they can replace their losses. This is why the individually superior Garou avoid wars with vampires. If the KJ start sending men at the Cainites, they're just handing them soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou is a dying race, so they avoid vampires, which are not their archenemies, at all costs.<br /> <br /> WG is... they increase faster and faster when the Sixth Age is coming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 08-24-2020, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T08:50:16-07:00","id":1410078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410074#post1410074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't matter how great KJ powers synergize: Cainites, if they're willing, can easily set the stage to be 2 versus 1, or 3 vs 1, or if they can branch out and make it 5 vs 1, or 10 vs 1, or 30 to 1 if they're really desperate. So long as there are people and one cainite remains alive, they can replace their losses. This is why the individually superior Garou avoid wars with vampires. If the KJ start sending men at the Cainites, they're just handing them soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not really. I mean this doesn't even work in a &quot;Sabbat vs Cam&quot; quality. You don't instantly get someone with 3 discipline dots with humanity 7 or on a path. You get something in frenzy just as likely to eat eachother as they are to attack the Wan Guei, possibly more so since Kindred are extra delicious to eachother. It takes time and training to be a worthwhile kindred its why PCs represent something that's gone through the accounting generally(or group equivalent)<br /> <br /> Garou GENERALLY don't war with Kindred because Kindred are good at hiding and Garou have alot of other shit to do(like murder their allies)...<br /> <br /> <br /> The real advantage Kindred have are Ghouls and the Blood bond. Making someone relatively loyal and more surivable than your average human with as much resourses spent as another kindred. This lets you turn even the most loyal ally or kinfolk against them.. Now that's real power. The embrace? that's just a neat trick, but if we want to play that game I could probably get more Ratkin through their rites of passage in a year than you could train up kindred to pc status and no one ever talks about how Ratkin rule everything...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T09:02:30-07:00","id":1410080,"title":"","content":"The embrace actually bolsters your attributes to a minimum of 7/5/3; says so in the section about ghouls getting embraced. As for the frenzy, they only frenzy upon the embrace when they're starving. You could embrace criminals or ex-military (plentiful in many regions with conscription) or take hunters or martial artists or... you can give base-military competence in only a couple of weeks. The Cathayans can't contend with that. Even if they're getting more second breaths, they still need to reel them in and return them to sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T09:38:25-07:00","id":1410086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410080#post1410080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The embrace actually bolsters your attributes to a minimum of 7/5/3; says so in the section about ghouls getting embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>if we're using v20 rules cainites, then cainites are toast (nerfed thaumaturgy and disciplines)<br /> <br /> in revised (the latest edition having rules for kj), new embraces didn't get more than 1 discipline (Children of the Night, mostly ignored rule though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T12:45:25-07:00","id":1410111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410010#post1410010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On the contrary. I never understood the idea of Hungry Dead as uber vamps, mechanically Cainites get stronger faster and grow their disciplines far more readily than the Hungry Dead can. They are also much more physically robust over all unless the Hungry Ghost embraces their demon side completely.<br /> <br /> As a species Cainites have the ability to reproduce at an exponential rate and can create utterly loyal mortal+ armies essentially on a whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you approach the question from a rules angle. Which is entirely valid.<br /> <br /> The writers presented things differently, though. They never went into much detail, so it's an Informed Attribute, but most of the core of KotE and works from Masquerade I remember playing up the Wan Gui as oh-so superior to the Stupid Gwailo vampires, in a really off-putting way.<br /> <br /> And I believe that has to do with the tone of V:tM. Wan Gui were thought up as something to scare western vampires with, because a large part of Vampire is about the world being filled with terrible, alien things the average vampire should be scared of, with the PCs usually beginning at the bottom of the totem pole.<br /> <br /> I'm not knocking that, I'm mainly wondering if KotE would flip the script, so to speak, if it was the core game and Cainites only later became playable (if at all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T13:06:42-07:00","id":1410117,"title":"","content":"Broadly speaking, East Asians are very much more racist than most of the rest of the world. The oh-so-superior attitude, off-putting as it may be, seems very fitting for them. <br /> If Kindred were asian and the hungry dead were the rest of the world, i'd expect the Cainites to have the smug superior attitudes and the rest of the world to be put off/horrified by them. <br /> If KotE remained asian but was the core game... I dunno; Are we going with Asian writers for an asian audience or white orientalists? Asian writers would likely stress the vampires of the bitter colonial years and somewhat ham up the european cainites (much like we've hammed them up) whilst white orientalists would probably stick to hamming the Orient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T13:41:07-07:00","id":1410126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410117#post1410117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly speaking, East Asians are very much more racist than most of the rest of the world. The oh-so-superior attitude, off-putting as it may be, seems very fitting for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, they actually could be superior and thus their point of view is justified. Then again those who don't know an answer often consider those who do understand such things to have superior than thou attitudes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410117#post1410117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Kindred were asian and the hungry dead were the rest of the world, i'd expect the Cainites to have the smug superior attitudes and the rest of the world to be put off/horrified by them.If KotE remained asian but was the core game... I dunno; Are we going with Asian writers for an asian audience or white orientalists? Asian writers would likely stress the vampires of the bitter colonial years and somewhat ham up the european cainites (much like we've hammed them up) whilst white orientalists would probably stick to hamming the Orient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or we could just look at how anime and manga have messed with European vampire legends. All the vampires would more akin to Helsing or Darkstalkers. About the only European aspects about them are the names and the excessive use of lace &amp; ruffles on the costumes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T15:44:09-07:00","id":1410145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410117#post1410117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly speaking, East Asians are very much more racist than most of the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Just a wee bit of a broad brush here, MyWifeIsScary.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking don't refer to groups like this.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410126#post1410126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, they actually could be superior and thus their point of view is justified. Then again those who don't know an answer often consider those who do understand such things to have superior than thou attitudes.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Not helping.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T16:49:41-07:00","id":1410157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410145#post1410145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Not helping.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, which part is not helping?<br /> <br /> The fact that White Wolf canonically stated in Kindred of the East that all asians are of a different spiritual content than all other humans on the planet, being the descendants of a magical sub-species of human / corrupted dragon-blooded. This is why the asian souls can go to the Yomi and end up creating broken mirror areas in asian communities in foreign lands. Thus a heritage of magic wielding people as portrayed in the WoD technically makes them superior to other bloodlines of humans in the setting as written.<br /> <br /> Or is the concept that I pointed out that racism is highly subjective and that our own society has gotten twitchy to the point of being hysterical about anything being considered racist, regardless if it actually is? It is sadly not uncommon for people to claim a view point is racist when they don't understand it or they are intimidated by it, or perhaps worst of all because they are scared of being seen as racist for not condemning anything remotely even close to racist views as a form of virtue signaling.<br /> <br /> Though it would be an interesting thought experiment to see exactly what would by our definition of racism, count as racist when looking at asian media representations of European cultures in anime/manga. Yes this runs a bit close to the subject of reverse racism or the idea of not being able to be racist against whites/europeans, but gaining perspective is always a worthy thing to pursue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T16:55:39-07:00","id":1410160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410080#post1410080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The embrace actually bolsters your attributes to a minimum of 7/5/3; says so in the section about ghouls getting embraced. As for the frenzy, they only frenzy upon the embrace when they're starving. You could embrace criminals or ex-military (plentiful in many regions with conscription) or take hunters or martial artists or... you can give base-military competence in only a couple of weeks. The Cathayans can't contend with that. Even if they're getting more second breaths, they still need to reel them in and return them to sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. Insults. Fire. Damage.Bright lights. These are things that it takes a neonate some training to get used to handling. Its why Shovelheads surviving is such a RARE thing. IF this really were a good plan then.. why didn't the Ravnos do it for thousands of years and when they started it.. was at best a mixed result and a worse caused the Week of Nightmares for them. Mass embraces aren't about making a legion of fighting vampires but about shitting in someone elses lawn and forcing them to clean it up.<br /> <br /> This is before the fact that Kindred are intrinsically more likely to betray each other. This is why the Sabbat has to blood bond themselves to eachother to keep anything functional. But yeah you could embrace a small military unit that was highly professional.. but those are of limited scale.. and probably ends up with a couple fewer elders in the end. Really.. now Ghouls Ghouls are wheere its at. No Frenzy, just some super powers and they kick in right away; You can have them guard your haven. Fight enemies during the day and its something that generally won't self destruct as long as you have blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T17:09:52-07:00","id":1410162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410111#post1410111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because you approach the question from a rules angle. Which is entirely valid.<br /> <br /> The writers presented things differently, though. They never went into much detail, so it's an Informed Attribute, but most of the core of KotE and works from Masquerade I remember playing up the Wan Gui as oh-so superior to the Stupid Gwailo vampires, in a really off-putting way.<br /> <br /> And I believe that has to do with the tone of V:tM. Wan Gui were thought up as something to scare western vampires with, because a large part of Vampire is about the world being filled with terrible, alien things the average vampire should be scared of, with the PCs usually beginning at the bottom of the totem pole.<br /> <br /> I'm not knocking that, I'm mainly wondering if KotE would flip the script, so to speak, if it was the core game and Cainites only later became playable (if at all).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very true.<br /> <br /> Its just something I've noted over the decades of running KotE is that HD, especially when young, really need to be very careful around Cainites as the damn things are much more robust than your average beginning Hungry Dead. But my campaigns never really rise above street level, I think the highest level campaign I got to was the end stage of a small mixed group of HD and Kindred going from town to town trying to find a safe haven and in the process almost circumnavigating Australias coast.<br /> <br /> Most of them are hard scrabble survival games in places like Bengkulu, Samarinda, Port Moresby, Bougainville etc. we never really get into the high level stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T17:18:12-07:00","id":1410165,"title":"","content":"You know, this scenario doesn't have to involve any sort of East versus West conflict. If the hungry dead are the dominant form of vampire across the world and have been so for millennia, then they would be as natural to Europe as they are to Eastern Asia. Vampires would escape from Hell, normally perceived in a Christian sense, and inhabit their undead bodies. The Yin, Yang, and Po would be referred to with different terms, likely involving the trappings of Western religion or spirituality. <br /> <br /> In fact, the traditional mythic vampire of Europe is more similar to a Kuei-jin than a Kindred. Traditional European vampire myths usually involved a person who died and then arose from the grave because of something bad about their life or death - not being transformed by another vampire. <br /> <br /> In this alternative setting, nobody would see these vampires as inherently Asian, they are just the kind of vampires you have everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T17:46:31-07:00","id":1410169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410157#post1410157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to be clear, which part is not helping</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Very well.<br /> <br /> Any book that maintains one race is superior to another in White Wolf's World of Darkness (WoD: Gypsies or Kindred of the East) is against the forum rules even though is official product and not to be taken seriously or discussed with anything other than derision.<br /> <br /> It was a bad idea, old shame, and is not what this forum or the vision of this game is about.<br /> <br /> Also, please PM disagreements with mod decisions not post them.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T18:07:15-07:00","id":1410171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410165#post1410165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, this scenario doesn't have to involve any sort of East versus West conflict. If the hungry dead are the dominant form of vampire across the world and have been so for millennia, then they would be as natural to Europe as they are to Eastern Asia. Vampires would escape from Hell, normally perceived in a Christian sense, and inhabit their undead bodies. The Yin, Yang, and Po would be referred to with different terms, likely involving the trappings of Western religion or spirituality.<br /> <br /> In fact, the traditional mythic vampire of Europe is more similar to a Kuei-jin than a Kindred. Traditional European vampire myths usually involved a person who died and then arose from the grave because of something bad about their life or death - not being transformed by another vampire.<br /> <br /> In this alternative setting, nobody would see these vampires as inherently Asian, they are just the kind of vampires you have everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correctamundo.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T19:27:11-07:00","id":1410188,"title":"","content":"Heh. Makes 'em sound like cockroaches, Damian. Multiply quickly and hard to kill. I actually like the idea of a crossover game like that. I hear Cainites and Wan Gui actually complement each other well.<br /> <br /> And Sergeant Brother, I agree. It's a really important design decision. The OP did specify them working under the traditional Kuei-Jin paradigm, though, it should be said; not different variations of dying and returning from a hell but everyone going to Yomi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T19:46:28-07:00","id":1410195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410188#post1410188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Makes 'em sound like cockroaches, Damian. Multiply quickly and hard to kill. I actually like the idea of a crossover game like that. I hear Cainites and Wan Gui actually complement each other well.<br /> <br /> And Sergeant Brother, I agree. It's a really important design decision. The OP did specify them working under the traditional Kuei-Jin paradigm, though, it should be said; not different variations of dying and returning from a hell but everyone going to Yomi.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but different cultures will flavor how they view the Thousand Hells. For example among the Abrahamic Religions, the Thousand Hells could be seen as one Hell made up of a thousand domains, ruled over demon lord subordinates to Lucifer.<br /> <br /> Hell, what if part of the reason the HD existence was able to spread was that the Yama Kings sought to expand their influence across the world, adopting the aspects and guises from figures from beliefs and myths outside of Eastern Asia, spreading their taint and corruption. And of course, others following in the footsteps of Mikaboshi (a mortal that managed to become a Yama King) and Emma-O (an entity that became corrupted into a Yama King), and adding non-Asian Hells to that realm and in turn, furthering it's reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T20:16:52-07:00","id":1410203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410188#post1410188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Makes 'em sound like cockroaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may have been a term used by a certain Garkain HD Elder in one of my campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T20:21:44-07:00","id":1410205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1409126-what-if-wan-gui-were-the-dominant-group-of-vampires-and-cainites-the-minority?p=1410195#post1410195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True but different cultures will flavor how they view the Thousand Hells. For example among the Abrahamic Religions, the Thousand Hells could be seen as one Hell made up of a thousand domains, ruled over demon lord subordinates to Lucifer.<br /> <br /> Hell, what if part of the reason the HD existence was able to spread was that the Yama Kings sought to expand their influence across the world, adopting the aspects and guises from figures from beliefs and myths outside of Eastern Asia, spreading their taint and corruption. And of course, others following in the footsteps of Mikaboshi (a mortal that managed to become a Yama King) and Emma-O (an entity that became corrupted into a Yama King), and adding non-Asian Hells to that realm and in turn, furthering it's reach.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T00:32:34-07:00","id":1410241,"title":"","content":"It's not a race thing, it's a culture thing. The Japanese are still lead by a right wing nationalist, they whitewash Imperial Japan's history in schools, most of asia doesn't like them because they act like they did nothing wrong, they Ignore their indigenous populations, they remain notoriously xenophobic (their attitudes are pretty good to white westerners) and anti imigration... <br /> <br /> and that's just Japan, a place we have good perceptions of. Taiwan liberalized only a few decades ago, SE asia has it's own problems, and there are two very promenent dictatorships routinely trying to instil traditional values and setting their populace against external and internal enemies. <br /> <br /> Obviously it's not a race thing. You could attribute it to a deep sense of paternalism, that most countries in the region have very right wing economic systems, the influence of ancient philosophers, historical factors such as modernity being thrusted against them by foreign powers rather than evolved...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","